fix(docking,interaction): guarantee drag completion and top-left floating anchor

Fix remaining stuck-state bug and floating horizontal jump:
- Track WM_EXITSIZEMOVE in WpfMessageDockingEventSource and invoke EnsureDragCompletedAfterNativeMove in WpfDockWindowHost.BeginDrag finally block (main and replica hosts) so clicks without movement never leave _dragging stuck true.
- Update DockPlacementCalculator.GetFloatingBounds to keep X, Y fixed (top-left anchor without recentering) and set TabBorderStyle to Left/Top in floating mode so the idle icon+name stays stationary and the deployed bar starts at the exact same X.
- Update floating placement tests and add TabBorderStyle_InFloatingMode_AnchorsTopLeft (500/500 passing in Debug and Release).

Refs: RF01, RF02, HU01, HU02, E2-CA1, E3-CA1, E3-CA2, ADR-005